D MLE ARE BOTH OPTIMAL FOR TOP-K RANKING},\n volume = {47},\n year = {2017}\n}\n\n@Article{Cook2000DetectionOI,\n author = {R. Cook},\n booktitle = {Technometrics},\n journal = {Technometrics},\n pages = {65 - 68},\n title = {Detection of Influential Observation in Linear Regression},\n volume = {42},\n year = {2000}\n}\n\n@Article{Davidson1970OnET,\n author = {R. Davidson},\n journal = {Journal of the American Statistical Association},\n pages = {317-328},\n title = {On Extending the Bradley-Terry Model to Accommodate Ties in Paired Comparison Experiments},\n volume = {65},\n year = {1970}\n}\n\n@Article{Ma2022ATO,\n author = {Ke Ma and Qian-Qian Xu and Jinshan Zeng and Guo-Rong Li and Xiaochun Cao and Qingming Huang},\n booktitle = {IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence},\n journal = {IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence},\n pages = {4090-4108},\n title = {A Tale of HodgeRank and Spectral Method: Target Attack Against Rank Aggregation is the Fixed Point of Adversarial Game},\n volume = {45},\n year = {2022}\n}\n\n@Article{Moitra2022ProvablyAO,\n author = {Ankur Moitra and Dhruv Rohatgi},\n booktitle = {International Conference on Learning Representations},\n journal = {ArXiv},\n title = {Provably Auditing Ordinary Least Squares in Low Dimensions},\n volume = {abs/2205.14284},\n year = {2022}\n}\n\n@Article{Dubois2024LengthControlledAA,\n author = {Yann Dubois and Bal'azs Galambosi and Percy Liang and Tatsunori Hashimoto},\n booktitle = {arXiv.org},\n journal = {ArXiv},\n title = {Length-Controlled AlpacaEval: A Simple Way to Debias Automatic Evaluators},\n volume = {abs/2404.04475},\n year = {2024}\n}\n\n@Article{Boubdir2023EloUR,\n author = {Meriem Boubdir and Edward Kim and B. Ermi{\\c{s}} and Sara Hooker and Marzieh Fadaee},\n booktitle = {IEEE Games Entertainment Media Conference},\n journal = {ArXiv},\n title = {Elo Uncovered: Robustness and Best Practices in Language Model Evaluation},\n volume = {abs/2311.17295},\n year = {2023}\n}\n\n@Article{Efron1979BootstrapMA,\n author = {B. Efron},\n journal = {Annals of Statistics},\n pages = {1-26},\n title = {Bootstrap Methods: Another Look at the Jackknife},\n volume = {7},\n year = {1979}\n}\n\n@Article{Shah2015SimpleRA,\n author = {Nihar B. Shah and M. Wainwright},\n booktitle = {Journal of machine learning research},\n journal = {ArXiv},\n title = {Simple, Robust and Optimal Ranking from Pairwise Comparisons},\n volume = {abs/1512.08949},\n year = {2015}\n}\n\n@Article{Basu2020InfluenceFI,\n author = {S. Basu and Phillip E. Pope and S. Feizi},\n booktitle = {International Conference on Learning Representations},\n journal = {ArXiv},\n title = {Influence Functions in Deep Learning Are Fragile},\n volume = {abs/2006.14651},\n year = {2020}\n}\n# Global Memory Summary\n\nUse as qualitative context only; do not use as quantitative grounding source.\n\n## Recent Entries\n\n- 2026-10-28T23:30:00Z | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: Cycle 1 idea: exchangeable-row categories mean counts on p x p stats; relinearized Frank-Wolfe/knapsack greedy over category counts, multi (insider,outsider) pair targeting, exact-refit pruning, starter AMIP fallback. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=no evaluation evidence yet.\n  - evidence: Starter program_0 uses one-shot AMIP ranking on k vs k+1 margin only; incumbent combined_score=0.0 correct=true; no runs in idea stage.\n- 2026-10-28T23:55:00Z | step=implement | scope=attempt\n  - summary: Implemented relinearized category knapsack: _build_categories/_stats_from_counts category refits, _relinearized_greedy damped knapsack steps, _candidate_pairs multi-pair targeting, _prune_counts exact pruning, _verify_rows row-level safety check, _baseline_amip starter fallback (new set used only if strictly smaller and verified).\n  - evidence: not executed; awaiting harness evaluation\n- 2026-10-28T23:40:00Z | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: Cycle 2 idea: resubmit category-count relinearized multi-pa