bility under data perturbation\", \"sensitivity of Bradley-Terry rankings\"). These risk surfacing the forbidden prior study or pages that cite it, so they are excluded by the task rules. The component-literature queries above cover the same ground without that risk.\n- **Generic queries** (\"robust optimization\", \"LLM benchmarking survey\", \"machine learning evaluation\"). They have low precision and no tie to influence, BT, or manipulation.\n- **Knapsack / Frank-Wolfe / relinearization queries.** These describe the untested variants and are not grounded by any evaluated result.\n- **Chronology / infra queries.** Excluded per the planning rules.\n\n## Forbidden patterns\nSee `forbidden_query_patterns` in the JSON: title copies of the research question, \"who cites / follow-ups of Huang et al.\" queries, generic filler, chronology or variant-name queries, and queries that present untested variants as validated.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
